Chapter: DeskSheetPointTest
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopPrograms
  cites Works chapter GopFont
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites UI chapter Layout
  cites Foreword chapter CCE

 WHERE TO CLICK. This lays the chrome and the start menu at the capture
 geometry and prints widget centres in DEVICE pixels.

 THE CAUSE WAS `desk-chrome-with`, NOT THE FACE, and the difference
 matters because the obvious repair does not work. This arm answered
 `menu` centre 156,848 at 1600x900 while the pill on the glass sits at
 x 34..147, so every click written from it missed on x and read exactly
 like a bed that delivers no clicks. It cost six captures. Handing the
 face to `desk-menu-tree` changes NOTHING for that number, measured
 2026-09-08 with a real ESP attached: `desk-chrome-with` is
 `desk-chrome-face content w ds gfont-none`, so the chrome the pill
 lives in discards any face its caller holds. Laying through
 `desk-chrome-face` with the face is what moved it.

 AND THE NUMBERS NOW LAND. Measured on the glass at head, the pill
 occupies x 34..147 and y 830..856, and the arm answers 90,848; the
 Sheets row occupies x 58..229 and y 510..533, and the arm answers
 144,526. Both are inside their widget on both axes.

 WITHOUT A MEDIUM THE CENTRES ARE WITHHELD. `desk-font` answers the
 fallback when nothing carries `CMUNSS.TTF`, and a centre laid on the
 fallback is not a click coordinate, so the arm prints the resolution
 check and refuses the numbers rather than offering one a reader would
 use. `build/desk.ps1` attaches such an ESP by default.

 The numbers are printed and asserted at once. A rect of zero width means
 `widget-find` did not find the id, which is the failure this would
 otherwise hand to a screenshot to discover.

Section: Body

  dsp-yn : Boolean -> Text
  dsp-yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "NO"

  dsp-box : WidgetNode, Text -> LayoutRect
  dsp-box (laid) (id) =
    when widget-find laid id
      is Just (n) -> n.wn-bounds
      is None -> layout-rect 0 0 0 0

  dsp-laid : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, GopFont -> WidgetNode
  dsp-laid (ds) (w) (h) (s) (tf) =
    widget-layout (desk-chrome-face (desk-menu-tree (peek-32 ds desk-prog-cell) tf s ds) w ds tf) (dk-theme-ds ds) (layout-rect 0 0 (w / s) (h / s))

  dsp-at : WidgetNode, Text, Integer -> Text
  dsp-at (laid) (id) (s) =
    let r = dsp-box laid id
    in id & " centre " & integer-to-text ((r.lr-x + r.lr-w / 2) * s) & "," & integer-to-text ((r.lr-y + r.lr-h / 2) * s)

  dsp-found : WidgetNode, Text -> Text
  dsp-found (laid) (id) =
    id & " found " & dsp-yn ((dsp-box laid id).lr-w > 0)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing = act
    let w = 1600
    in let h = 900
    in let ds = alloc-zeroed dk-ds-bytes 64
    in let ps = alloc-zeroed 64 64
    in let pp = poke-32 ds desk-prog-cell ps
    in let e = gpr-ensure ps
    in let s = ui-wscale w
    in act
      tf <- desk-font w
      let laid = dsp-laid ds w h s tf
      in act
        print-line-uni ("scale " & integer-to-text s)
        print-line-uni (dsp-found laid "menu")
        print-line-uni (dsp-found laid "gpr-Sheets")
        print-line-uni (dsp-found laid "gpr-Clock")
        if tf.gf-ok == False then
          print-line-uni ("no TrueType face on the medium, so the centres are withheld")
        else act
          print-line-uni (dsp-at laid "menu" s)
          print-line-uni (dsp-at laid "gpr-Sheets" s)
          print-line-uni (dsp-at laid "gpr-Clock" s)
        end
      end
    end
  end
